    "question": "36 liters of diesel fuel is worth €18. The tank of this pickup truck can hold 64 liters. How much does a full tank of diesel fuel cost?",
    "gold": "32",
    "answer": "A liter of diesel costs 18/ 36 = <<18/36=0.5>>0.5 €.\n64 liters of diesel fuel cost 0.5 X 64 = <<64*0.5=32>>32 €\n#### 32"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the cost of a full tank of diesel fuel for the pickup truck, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the cost of 1 liter of diesel fuel:**\n   - We know that 36 liters of diesel fuel is worth €18.\n   - To find the cost of 1 liter, we divide the total cost by the number of liters:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Cost per liter} = \\frac{18 \\text{ euros}}{36 \\text{ liters}} = \\frac{18}{36} = \\frac{1}{2} \\text{ euros per liter}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the cost of 64 liters of diesel fuel:**\n   - Now that we know the cost of 1 liter is €0.50, we can find the cost of 64 liters by multiplying:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Cost of 64 liters} = 64 \\text{ liters} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\text{ euros per liter} = 64 \\times 0.5 = 32 \\text{ euros}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of a full tank of diesel fuel is \\(\\boxed{32}\\) euros.",
